# dependencies / build output
node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/

# env
.env
.env*.local

# Reference material only — the extracted static site, blueprint PDF and
# spreadsheet. Kept out of the repo because the two TVC videos inside are
# 202 MB and 160 MB, well past GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit. The folder on
# disk is named "recource"; the old "korbo group" line never matched it.
recource/
korbo group/

# Money receipts that were dropped into public/images by mistake. They carry
# personal and financial details and would be served by the site if committed.
client/public/images/MoneyReceipt*

# editor / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log

# Client reference material — Illustrator masters, 500 MB apiece. Past
# GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit outright, and once in the history the repo
# carries the weight even after a delete. Named rather than globbed as `*.ai`
# so a small artwork file can still be committed deliberately.
Company profile 1-32 page for agency.ai
Foam Catalogue .ai
Mattress Catalogue (1).ai

# Client catalogue source (Adobe/PDF) and the lightweight page renders of the
# mattress catalogue extracted from it. Reference material, kept on disk but
# out of the repo — the brochure alone is ~68 MB of page PNGs.
Karmo Adhesive Catalog.pdf
Mattress Brochure/

# Raw image drops that land in the project root on their way in — generator
# output, phone photos, screenshots. Anything the site actually uses is
# converted into client/public/karmo/images/ under a name that says what it
# is, and the master is filed under recource/originals/ (also ignored). What
# is left here is a staging area, 3-7 MB a file, and belongs in neither.
# Any loose image at the repo root, whatever it is called — the named patterns
# this replaced kept missing new ones (BG1.jpg, a stock filename in Cyrillic
# transliteration). Nothing is meant to live here: site assets go under
# client/public/karmo/images/ and masters under recource/originals/.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.webp

# Installers and other binaries that land in the working folder by accident.
*.exe
